If you accidentally press the dictation or voice icon after sending a text in Messages, your music may pause while your iPhone starts listening. It's a small annoyance, but a frequent one, since the dictation/audio icon sits so close to the send arrow that stray taps are almost inevitable. In iOS 27 and iPadOS 27, Apple has finally given you a way to get rid of it.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/messages-dictation-ios.jpeg" alt="messages" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1058036" /><br/>
The issue is one that popstar Justin Bieber publicly <a href="https://www.instagram.com/lilbieber/p/DR3EK3OkmOF/">complained</a> about, claiming that the send button shouldn't have multiple functions so close together. The post went viral, and in iOS 27, Apple has done something about it.<br/>
<br/>
Quite simply, the message text field now has a new setting. You can choose whether it displays the audio waveform icon for recording a voice message, the microphone icon for dictation, or nothing at all. Here's how to find it:<br/>
<ol><br/>
  <li>Open the <strong>Settings</strong> app on your iPhone or iPad.</li><br/>
  <li>Tap <strong>Apps</strong> at the bottom of the list.</li><br/>
  <li>Tap <strong>Messages</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Tap <strong>Show in Text Field</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Choose one of the three options: <strong>Record Audio</strong>, <strong>Start Dictation</strong>, or <strong>None</strong>.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/turn-off-dictation-voice-icon-messages.jpeg" alt="settings" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1058040" /><br/>
</ol>If you keep tapping the text field icon by mistake, you'll want to choose <strong>None</strong>.<br/>
<br/>
If you occasionally record voice messages, don't worry – you can still use the plus button to the left of the input field to enable <strong>Audio</strong>. If it's dictation you sometimes use, you'll find the microphone key at the bottom right of the iOS keyboard (if it's not there, go to <strong>Settings ➝ General ➝ Keyboard</strong> and turn on <strong>Enable Dictation</strong>.)<br/>
<br/>
